#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# mod

#% text
# `mod(a, m)` gives the remainder of `a` on division by `m`, with the sign of `m`.

#% text
# `mod(a, m, d)` gives the remainder shifted to lie between `d` and `d + m`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `mod(a, m)` is `a - m*floor(a/m)`, so for `m > 0` it lies in 0, ..., `m` - 1 and is never negative.

#% item
# `mod(a, m, d)` is `a - m*floor((a - d)/m)`; `mod(a, m, 1)` lies in 1, ..., `m`.

#% item
# `a` and `m` may be integers, fractions or machine reals.

#% item
# `mod` is listable: it applies to each element of a list.

#% item
# `m` = 0 gives a division-by-zero failure.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
mod(17, 5)
#% output
#= 2

#% text
# The remainder of a negative number is still between 0 and `m` - 1:

#% cell
mod(-17, 5)
#% output
#= 3

#% text
# The sign follows `m`:

#% cell
mod(17, -5)
#% output
#= -3

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# An offset: remainders from 1 to 5 instead of 0 to 4:

#% cell
mod(10, 5, 1)
#% output
#= 5

#% text
# Fractions and machine reals:

#% cell
mod(7/2, 1)
#% output
#= 1/2

#% cell
mod(5.5, 2)
#% output
#= 1.5

#% cell
mod(-1.5, 1.0)
#% output
#= 0.5

#% text
# Each element of a list:

#% cell
mod(range(6), 3)
#% output
#= [1, 2, 0, 1, 2, 0]

#% text
# Large integers:

#% cell
mod(10^30 + 7, 10)
#% output
#= 7

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# The fractional part of a ball:

#% cell
mod(n(pi, 30), 1)
#% output
#= 0.1415926535897932384626433832795029

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# The quotient and the remainder rebuild the number:

#% cell
quotient(17, 5)*5 + mod(17, 5)
#% output
#= 17

#% text
# `power_mod` gives the same remainder without forming the large power:

#% cell
[mod(3^100, 7), power_mod(3, 100, 7)]
#% output
#= [4, 4]

#% subsection
# Possible issues

#% text
# A remainder modulo 0 is undefined:

#% cell
mod(7, 0)
#% output
#! failure(division_by_zero)

#% text
# A modulus with an irrational value is not reduced:

#% cell
mod(2pi + 1, 2pi)
#% output
#= mod(1 + 2*pi, 2*pi)

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `quotient`, `floor`, `power_mod`, `gcd`
